Semantics: loop1 sets a[i]=i. loop2 sets b[N-i-1]=i (so b[k] = N-1-k for k in 0..N-1). loop3 accumulates sum += a[i]-b[N-i-1], which is i - (N-1-(N-i-1)) = i - i = 0, so sum stays 0.

HARD CONSTRAINTS:
1. Do NOT modify any original C token. Only ADD ACSL comment annotations. The final annotated file must preserve loops and `//@assert(sum == 0);` exactly.
